g football player  who's you know maybe  said some things on radio and twitter  that maybe he shouldn't have and i i  think that is yeah the perception of him  i think through the league was oh maybe  he's not happy with the jets maybe he  wants to get out of there uh but uh  certainly you know joe douglas adam gase  the one thing i'll say about both of  those guys and i i know adam i don't  know joe douglas all that well but know  a lot of people that know him and the  one thing you know about adam and really  anybody that's around him in coach gates  is just the fact that they're not bsers  i mean they lay it on the line i mean we  just saw earlier in you know in one of  our pods adam gates saying hey the  results are what they are right now  we're not good and i'm not doing a good  job because we only have one win you  know he'll take it on the chin like a  true champ and yeah i can't fault them  for just at least listening to offers  and things like that now you got to blow  them out of the water because jamal  adams is i you could argue jamal adam's  the best safety in football he's  certainly in that conversation uh but  but yeah they took some calls they  listened to what people have to say and  maybe if the team offered them two  first-round picks or something like that  maybe they would have done it but that  was not offered and uh for that they  keep keep the safety who who will be a  superstar uh for a long long time here  in new york  cowboys reportedly offered a first round  pick and an early third day pick a  fourth or a fifth rounder for adams the  jets rejected that and the ravens  reportedly were in contact and actively  proceed pursuing jamal adams and there's  a thought that maybe after the season  the ravens will try again and you can  keep trying all you want until you offer  the jets enough to get them to say we'll  do it they're not going to do it and and  you know why would you trade jamal adams  well again if you can get a great haul  of draft picks in return and you decide  it's fair value then you do it and and  also chris there's just been enough  flash points from jamal adams over the  past few years remember it seemed like  todd bowles had to talk to him every  other week right in 2018 and adam gase  has gotten that part of it under control  it doesn't seem like jamal adams is  saying things that are unfortunate  problematic for the team but nobody  knows him better than the jets and the  mere fact that they would even have  those conversations and entertain those  offers it tells you that at some point  they they recognize maybe he's not  somebody who needs to be with this  franchise over the long haul maybe he's  not a guy to build around because of the  fact that he is a little temperamental  that he does you know we played at the  very top of the tv segment as the hour  began le'veon bell talking about how the  jets are a work in progress and it's  going to take time you know jamal adams  was basically despondent after they lost  to the jaguars on sunday and and maybe  they're maybe they're thinking look he's  a great player but the culture we're  trying to build isn't somebody who's  going to have highs that are too high  and lows that are too low but somebody  who's more even keeled and understands  that this really is a process i'm just  trying to yeah to process why they would  even entertain these discussions and it  may be at some level they were kind of  hoping they would be made an offer they  can't refuse well maybe you know yeah  you know we don't know that uh either  way they're listening to it i mean  you're right about jamal adams i do  think he's got to dial back you know  some of the emotional outbursts i love  watching him play uh i think he's a  great dude he's got great energy  i've been around him a few times and i  mean you could see how uh he's the  perfect guy to be uh safety a strong  safety in the nfl yeah he i mean even  when you're just around him in a normal  everyday setting he's intense and you  could tell he loves football but yeah  he's got to worry about maybe crossing  that line too much to where it becomes  yeah a little bit of the hot the highs  are too high the lows are too low to  where it affects the locker room i don't  think the jets ultimately wanted to  trade him the jets don't have that many  good players and you could argue he's  maybe the best player on the team and if  you want to rebuild you'd like to keep  those guys around especially when  they're very young still like adams is  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

